hadiths[282]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27004","Hushaim ibn Bashir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Subay ah bint Al-Harith gave birth twenty nights or about that after the death of her husband, and she wanted to marry, so Abu As-Sanabil said to her: That is not for you until the last of the two terms passes over you, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: She may marry when she wishes."
"27005","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Umm Salamah, she said: When Abu Salamah died I said: A stranger, and he died in a strange land, so I poured forth weeping, so a woman came wanting to help me wail from As-Sa id, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you want to bring the Satan into a house from which Allah the Mighty and Majestic has removed him, she said: So I did not weep over him."
"27006","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salamah, she mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has a mukatab and he has with him what he can pay, then let her veil herself from him."
"27007","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Humayd, he heard Said ibn Al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the ten enter and a man wants to sacrifice, then let him not touch any of his hair nor his skin."
"27008","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Suqah, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Umm Salamah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the army which will be swallowed up, so Umm Salamah said: Perhaps among them is one forced, so he said: They will be resurrected according to their intentions."
"27009","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar, meaning Ad-Duhni, he heard Abu Salamah informing from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The legs of my minbar are fixed in Paradise."
"27010","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Said, meaning Al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, and he is the freed slave of Umm Salamah, thus Sufyan said, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who tightens the braid of her head, he said: It suffices you to pour water over it three times."
"27011","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more hastening of Dhuhr than you, and you are more hastening of Asr than him."
"27012","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Al-A mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, he said: Aishah and Umm Salamah were asked which deed was most pleasing to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: That which is continued even if little."
"27013","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Hunaydah Al-Khuzai, from his mother, she said: I entered upon Umm Salamah and asked her about fasting, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command me to fast three days of every month, the first of them Monday and Friday and Thursday."
"27014","Abd Al-A la narrated to us, from Ma mar, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Harith ibn Hisham, he said: I and my father entered upon Aishah and Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the morning while junub then he would fast."
"27015","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I did not forget his saying on the day of Al-Khandaq while he was handing them milk and the hair of his chest had become dusty, and he was saying: O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah, he said: So he saw Ammar and said: Woe to him, son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill him, he said: So I mentioned it to Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, so he said: From his mother, I said: Yes, indeed she used to mix with her, visiting her."
"27016","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Safinah the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Among the last bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: The prayer, the prayer, and what your right hands possess, until the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stammered it in his chest and his tongue could not utter it."
"27017","Abdur-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us: Malik, from Sumayy and Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Aishah and Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the morning junub from intercourse, not a wet dream, then he would fast, and in the hadith of Abd Rabbihi: In Ramadan."
"27018","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu Al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she arrived while she was ill, so she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Circumambulate behind the people while you are riding, she said: So I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at the Ka bah, reciting At-Tur."
"27019","Jarir ibn Abd Al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with seven and with five, not separating between them with salam nor with speech."
"27020","Jarir narrated to us, from Abd Al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ubaydullah Ibn Al-Qibtiyyah, he said: Al-Harith ibn Abi Rabiah and Abdullah ibn Safwan entered, and I was with them, upon Umm Salamah, so they asked her about the army which will be swallowed up, and that was in the days of Ibn Az-Zubayr, so Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One seeking refuge will seek refuge at Al-Hijr, so Allah will send an army, and when they are at a desert plain of the earth they will be swallowed up, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, then how about one who was brought out unwillingly, he said: He will be swallowed up with them, but he will be resurrected according to his intention on the Day of Resurrection, so I mentioned that to Abu Jafar, so he said: It is the desert plain of Al-Madinah."
"27021","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from an umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, she said: I used to drag my hem and pass by the dirty place and the clean place, so I entered upon Umm Salamah and asked her about that, so she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What comes after it purifies it."
"27022","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon her, he said: So he said: O mother, I have feared that my abundant wealth will destroy me, I am the wealthiest of Quraysh in wealth, she said: O my son, then spend, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed among my companions is one who will not see me after I part from him, so he went out and met Umar and informed him, so Umar came and entered upon her, so he said to her: By Allah, am I among them, so she said: No, and I will not declare anyone innocent after you."
"27023","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while with her was an effeminate man, and with her was her brother Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, and the effeminate one was saying to Abdullah: O Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, if Allah grants you conquest of At-Taif tomorrow, then take to you the daughter of Ghaylan, for she comes with four and turns with eight, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him, so he said to Umm Salamah: This one shall not enter upon you."
"27024","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You dispute to me, and perhaps some of you is more eloquent in his proof than some, and I am only a man, I judge for him according to what I hear from him, so whoever I judge for him something of the right of his brother, then it is only fire, so let him not take it."
"27025","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to meet with him the Fajr prayer on the day of sacrifice at Makkah."
"27026","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Habibah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you want my sister, he said: What should I do with her, she said: Marry her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: And do you like that, so she said: Yes, I am not solely yours, and the most deserving to share with me in good is my sister, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful to me, she said: By Allah, it has reached me that you are betrothing Durrah bint Abi Salamah, daughter of Umm Salamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she were lawful to me I would not have married her, Thuwaybah the freed slave of Banu Hashim suckled me and her father, so do not offer to me your sisters nor your daughters."
"27027","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I said: Do you want my sister, so he mentioned the hadith."
"27028","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, she said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will you not marry my sister, so he mentioned the hadith."
"27029","Abu Al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from Az-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn Az-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him that Umm Habibah daughter of Abu Sufyan informed her that she said: O Messenger of Allah, marry my sister, so he mentioned the hadith, my father said: And the nephew of Az-Zuhri agreed with him, and Uqayl said: Indeed Umm Habibah said."
"27030","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend the dead or the sick, then say good, for the angels say amen to what you say, she said: So when Abu Salamah died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Salamah has died, so he said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and him, and grant me from him a good recompense, she said: So I said it, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic granted me one who is better to me than him, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27031","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham Ad-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash from one vessel from janabah, and he used to kiss her while fasting."
"27032","Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is present and prayer is present, then begin with supper."
"27033","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, he said: Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to me that a woman asked Umm Salamah and said: My husband kisses me while fasting and I am fasting, so what do you think, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss me while he was fasting and I was fasting."
"27034","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from her mother, that a woman whose husband died complained of her eye, so they mentioned her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned kohl, they said: We fear for her eye, he said: One of you used to remain in her house in her worst old garment, or in her old garments in the covering of her house, for a year, then when a dog passed by her she threw a dung, so will she not four months and ten."
"27035","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Zaynab daughter of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then Bilal came to him, so he went out to prayer and did not touch water."
"27036","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Zaynab daughter of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed Allah is not shy of the truth, is there ghusl upon the woman when she has a wet dream, he said: Yes, if she sees water, so Umm Salamah laughed, she said: Does a woman have a wet dream, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then how does the child resemble."
"27037","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Abd Al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married her, stayed with her three days, and said: You are not lowly to your family, if you wish I will stay seven with you, and if I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"27038","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Raytah narrated to me, from Kabshah daughter of Abi Maryam, she said: I said to Umm Salamah: Inform me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade his family, she said: He forbade us to chew date pits by cooking, and to mix raisins and dates."
"27039","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ammar Ad-Duhni narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The legs of the minbar are fixed in Paradise."
"27040","Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman ibn Muhammad, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman Abu Nasr, he said: Musawir Al-Himyari narrated to me, from his mother, she said: I heard Umm Salamah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: No believer hates you and no hypocrite loves you."
"27041","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Abd Al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: One who heard Umm Salamah narrated to me, mentioning that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in her house, so Fatimah came to him with a pot in it khazirah, so she entered with it upon him, so he said to her: Call your husband and your two sons, she said: So Ali and Al-Husayn and Al-Hasan came, so they entered upon him, so they sat eating from that khazirah, and he was upon a sleeping place of his upon a bench, under him a Khaybari cloak of his, she said: And I was praying in the room, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down this verse: Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you, people of the house, and purify you thoroughly, she said: So he took the excess of the cloak and covered them with it, then he took out his hand and pointed with it to the sky, then said: O Allah, these are my household and my special ones, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly, O Allah, these are my household and my special ones, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly, she said: So I put my head into the house and said: And I with you, O Messenger of Allah, he said: You are to good, you are to good."
"27042","Abd Al-Malik said: And Abu Layla narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, like the hadith of Ata exactly."
"27043","Abd Al-Malik said: And Dawud ibn Abi Awf Abu Al-Hajjaf narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, with the like of it exactly."
"27044","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab daughter of Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there reward for me regarding the sons of Abi Salamah, that I spend upon them, and I will not leave them thus and thus and thus, they are only my sons, he said: Yes, in them is reward, whatever you spend upon them."
"27045","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she sought a fatwa from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman whose blood flows, so he said: She waits the measure of the nights and days she used to menstruate, and their measure of the month, then she leaves prayer, then let her wash and wrap tightly, then pray."
"27046","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: Then how about women, O Messenger of Allah, he said: They lengthen a span, I said: Then it will be uncovered from them, he said: Then an arm, they shall not add over it."
"27047","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, informed us, from Awf ibn Al-Harith ibn At-Tufayl, from Rumaythah Umm Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: My companions spoke to me to speak to the Messenger of Allah to command the people to give gifts to him wherever he is, for they seek out with their gifts the day of Aishah, and we love good as Aishah loves it, so I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my companions spoke to me to speak to you to command the people to give gifts to you wherever you are, for the people seek out with their gifts the day of Aishah, and we only love good as Aishah loves, she said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent and did not answer me, so my companions came to me, so I informed them he did not speak to me, so they said: Do not leave him, and this is not a time to leave him, she said: Then he went around, so I spoke to him, so I said: My companions have commanded me to speak to you, command the people, let them give gifts to you wherever you are, so she said to him the like of that saying two or three times, each time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward her, then he said: O Umm Salamah, do not harm me regarding Aishah, for by Allah, revelation has not come down upon me while I am in the house of any woman of my wives except Aishah, so she said: I seek refuge with Allah from harming you regarding Aishah."
"27048","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Awf ibn Al-Harith, from his sister Rumaythah daughter of Al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: The people seek out with their gifts, so he mentioned its meaning."
"27049","Abu Al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd Al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while his face was pale, she said: So I thought that was from pain, so I said: O Prophet of Allah, what is with you, pale of face, he said: Because of the seven dinars which came to us yesterday, we entered evening while they were in the fold of the bedding."
"27050","Ya la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me after Asr and prayed two rakahs, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer, you did not use to pray it, he said: A delegation of Banu Tamim came and kept me from two rakahs I used to bow after Dhuhr."
"27051","Qurran ibn Tammam Abu Tammam Al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah Al-Makhzumi, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: O my son, shall I not narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I said: Yes, O mother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends upon two daughters or two sisters or female relatives, seeking reward for the spending upon them until Allah enriches them from His bounty the Mighty and Majestic, or suffices them, they will be for him a veil from the Fire."
"27052","Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Shaban and Ramadan."
"27053","Waki narrated to us, he said: Harun An-Nahwi narrated to us, from Thabit Al-Bunani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: Indeed he did unrighteous work."
"27054","Waki narrated to us, from Abd Al-Hamid ibn Bahram, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."
"27055","Waki narrated to us, Al-Qasim ibn Al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"27056","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of Fajr: O Allah, I ask You beneficial knowledge and accepted work and wholesome provision."
"27057","Waki and Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Wahb the freed slave of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she had not veiled, so he said: One veil, not two veils."
"27058","Waki narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in the room of Umm Salamah, so Abdullah or Umar passed in front of him, so he said with his hand thus, he said: So he returned, he said: So the daughter of Umm Salamah passed, so he said with his hand thus, he said: So she went on, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he said: They are predominant."
"27059","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Said narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah or Umm Salamah, Waki said: He doubted, meaning Abdullah ibn Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to one of them: An angel entered upon me in the house who had not entered upon me before it, so he said to me: This son of yours, Husayn, will be killed, and if you wish I will show you of the dust of the earth in which he will be killed, he said: So he brought out red dust."
"27060","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I menstruated while I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a garment, she said: So I slipped away, so he said: Have you menstruated, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I found what women find, he said: That is what was written upon the daughters of Adam, she said: So I went and fixed my affair, so I wrapped tightly with a garment, then I came and entered with him in his cover."
"27061","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad informed me, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Ya la ibn Mamlak, he said: I asked Umm Salamah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night and his recitation, so she said: What is with you and his prayer and his recitation, he used to pray the measure he slept and sleep the measure he prayed, and she was describing a recitation, explained, letter by letter."
"27062","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, from Mundhir Ath-Thawri, from Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, he said: A woman of the Ansar narrated to me, she is alive today, if you wish I will take you in to her, I said: No, narrate to me, she said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her as if angry, so I veiled myself from him with the sleeve of my shirt, so he spoke with speech I did not understand, so I said: O Mother of the Believers, as if I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter while angry, so she said: Yes, did you not hear what he said, I said: And what did he say, she said: He said: Indeed when evil spreads in the earth and is not forbidden, Allah the Mighty and Majestic sends His punishment upon the people of the earth, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and among them are the righteous, she said: He said: Yes, and among them are the righteous, what befell the people befalls them, then Allah the Mighty and Majestic takes them to His forgiveness and His pleasure, or to His pleasure and His forgiveness."
"27063","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Muhsin, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers, you will recognize and deny, so whoever denies has cleared himself, and whoever hates has become safe, but whoever is pleased and follows, they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them, he said: No, as long as they pray the five for you."
"27064","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit Al-Bunani, he said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to Umm Salamah, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none of my guardians, meaning present, so he said: There is none of your guardians present nor absent who dislikes that, so she said: O Umar, marry the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Indeed I will not give you less than what I gave your sisters, two hand mills and a jar and a cushion of leather stuffed with fiber, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to her to consummate with her, and when she saw him she took Zaynab her daughter and put her in her lap, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would leave, so Ammar ibn Yasir knew of that, and he was her brother through suckling, so he came to her and said: Where is this ill-fated, ugly one, by whom you have harmed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he took her and went with her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered upon her, so he cast his sight about the corners of the house, so he said: What did Zanab do, so she said: Ammar came and took her and went with her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated with her, and said to her: If you wish I will stay seven with you, if I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"27065","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah narrated to me, from his father and from his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, both of them narrating that to him from her, she said: My night in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to me was the evening of the day of sacrifice, she said: So he came to me, she said: So Wahb ibn Zamah entered upon me, and with him a man of the family of Abu Umayyah, wearing shirts, she said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Wahb: Have you poured forth yet, O Abu Abdullah, he said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Take off the shirt from you, he said: So he took it off from his head, and his companion took off his shirt from his head, then they said: And why, O Messenger of Allah, he said: This is a day in which it was permitted for you, when you have stoned the jamrah, to become lawful, meaning from all that was forbidden to you except women, when you enter evening before you circumambulate this House, you return unlawful as you were before you stoned the jamrah until you circumambulate it."
"27066","Muhammad said: Abu Ubaydah said: And Umm Qays daughter of Mihsan narrated to me, and she was their neighbor, she said: Ukkashah ibn Mihsan went out from me with a group of Banu Asad wearing shirts on the evening of the day of sacrifice, then they returned to me in the evening, their shirts upon their hands carrying them, she said: So I said: O Ukkashah, what is with you, you went out wearing shirts then returned with your shirts upon your hands carrying them, so he said: Umm Qays informed us, this was a day in which it was permitted for us, when we stoned the jamrah we became lawful from all that was forbidden to us except what was of women, until we circumambulate the House, so when we entered evening and did not circumambulate it, we became unlawful as we were before we stoned the jamrah until we circumambulate it, and we had not circumambulated, so we made our shirts as you see."
"27067","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hems of women a span, I said: Then their feet will show, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Then an arm, do not add over it."
"27068","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Qays, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss while fasting, so if she says no, then say to her: Aishah informs the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting, he said: So I asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss while fasting, she said: No, I said: Aishah informs the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting, she said: Perhaps he could not control himself from her out of love, as for me, then no."
"27069","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Qays the freed slave of Amr ibn Al-As narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al-As sent me to Umm Salamah, so he mentioned its meaning."
"27070","Hashim ibn Al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah, he said: We entered upon Umm Salamah, so she brought out to us some hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was dyed red with henna and katam."
"27071","Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Jafar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Habib, son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar, narrated to us, he said: A shaykh of Al-Madinah narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Prepare the sitting place for us, for an angel will descend to the earth who has never descended to it ever."
"27072","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Az-Zuhri, that Nabhan narrated to him that Umm Salamah narrated to him, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Maymunah, so Ibn Umm Maktum came until he entered upon him, and that was after he commanded us with hijab, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Veil yourselves from him, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, is he not blind, he does not see us nor know us, he said: Are you two blind, do you not see him."
"27073","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Wahb the freed slave of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was veiling, so he said: One veil, not two veils."
"27074","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, so she brought out to us hair of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dyed with henna and katam."
"27075","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Al-Muaddil Atiyyah At-Tufawi, from his father, that Umm Salamah narrated to him, she said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house one day, when the servant said: Ali and Fatimah are at the door, she said: So he said to me: Rise and move away from my household for me, she said: So I rose and moved away in the house nearby, so Ali and Fatimah entered, and with them Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn, and they were two small boys, so he took the two boys and put them in his lap and kissed them, he said: And he embraced Ali with one of his hands and Fatimah with the other hand, so he kissed Fatimah and kissed Ali, so he covered them with a black khamisah, so he said: O Allah, to You, not to the Fire, me and my household, she said: So I said: And I, O Messenger of Allah, so he said: And you."
"27076","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Hind bint Al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave salam, the women would stand when he finished his salam, and he would remain in his place a little before he stood."
"27077","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, Amr narrated to me, from Abu As-Samh, from As-Saib the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best mosques of women are the innermost of their houses."
"27078","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq, meaning Al-Fazari, narrated to us, from Khalid Al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Abu Salamah while his sight had opened, so he closed it, then said: When the soul is seized the sight follows it, so some people of his family cried out, so he said: Do not supplicate upon yourselves except with good, for the angels say amen to what you say, then he said: O Allah, forgive Abu Salamah and raise his rank among the guided, and leave him behind in his offspring among those remaining, and forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds, O Allah, make spacious in his grave and light for him in it."
"27079","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from his father, from Al-Aswad, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not taken until most of his prayer was sitting."
"27080","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Hind bint Al-Harith, Az-Zuhri said: And Hind had buttons in her sleeve, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up one night saying: There is no god but Allah, what treasures were opened tonight, there is no god but Allah, what trial was sent down tonight, who will wake the mistresses of the rooms, O many clothed in the world, naked in the Hereafter."
"27081","Abu Amir narrated to us, Aflah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Rafi narrated to us, he said: Umm Salamah used to narrate that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon the minbar while she was combing: O people, so she said to her hairdresser: Wrap my head, she said: So she said: May I be ransom for you, he only says: O people, I said: Woe to you, are we not of the people, so she wrapped her head and stood in her room, so she heard him saying: O people, while I am upon the Hawd, you will be brought in groups, then the paths will scatter you, so I will call you: Come to the path, so a caller will call me from after me, so he will say: They changed after you, so I will say: Away, away."
"27082","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, Abdur-Razzaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Ya la ibn Mamlak informed me that he asked Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, she said: He would pray the last Isha, then glorify, then pray after it what Allah willed of the night, then leave and sleep the like of what he prayed, then wake from that sleep of his, so pray the like of what he slept, and his last prayer would be to the morning."
"27083","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad Al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu Imran Aslam, that he said: I performed Hajj with my masters, so I entered upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: Shall I perform Umrah before I perform Hajj, she said: If you wish perform Umrah before you perform Hajj, and if you wish after you perform Hajj, he said: So I said: They say whoever was unmarried, it is not proper to perform Umrah before Hajj, he said: So I asked the mothers of the believers, so they said like what she said, so I returned to her and informed her of their saying, he said: So she said: Yes, and I will heal you, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Enter ihram, O family of Muhammad, with Umrah in Hajj."
"27084","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my companions is one whom I will not see nor will he see me after I die ever, he said: So that reached Umar, he said: So he came to her hurrying or hastening, Shadhan doubted, he said: So he said to her: I ask you by Allah, am I among them, she said: No, and I will never declare anyone innocent after you ever."
"27085","Abu An-Nadr Hashim ibn Al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd Al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Bahram, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the news of Al-Husayn ibn Ali came, she cursed the people of Iraq, so she said: They killed him, may Allah kill them, they deceived him and humiliated him, may Allah kill them, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Fatimah came to him in the morning with a pot in which she had made for him asidah, carrying it in a dish of hers until she put it before him, so he said to her: Where is your cousin, she said: He is in the house, he said: Go and call him and bring me his two sons, she said: So she came leading her two sons, each one of them by a hand, and Ali walking behind them, until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he seated them in his lap, and Ali sat on his right, and Fatimah sat on his left, Umm Salamah said: So she pulled from under me a Khaybari cloak which was a mat for us upon the sleeping place in Al-Madinah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped it upon them all, so he took with his left the two ends of the cloak and turned with his right hand to his Lord the Mighty and Majestic, he said: O Allah, my family, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly, O Allah, my household, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly, O Allah, my household, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly, I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I not of your family, he said: Yes, so enter into the cloak, she said: So I entered into the cloak after he finished his supplication for his cousin Ali and his two sons and his daughter Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"27086","Abu An-Nadr narrated to us, Abd Al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salamah narrating, she claimed that Fatimah came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining to him of service, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah my hands have blistered from the mill, I grind once and knead once, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: If Allah grants you something it will come to you, and I will guide you to better than that, when you keep your bed, then glorify Allah thirty-three and magnify thirty-three and praise thirty-four, so that is one hundred, so it is better for you than a servant, and when you pray the Fajr prayer, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, to Him is dominion and to Him is praise, He gives life and death, in His hand is good, and He is over all things Capable, ten times after Fajr prayer and ten times after Maghrib prayer, for each one of them will be written ten good deeds and remove ten evil deeds, and each one of them is like freeing a neck of the children of Ismail, and no sin earned that day may overtake him except shirk, there is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, and it is your guard between your saying it in the morning until you say it in the evening, from every Satan and every evil."
"27087","Abu An-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman the freed slave of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would become junub then sleep then wake then sleep."
"27088","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, Maymun ibn Musa Al-Marai narrated to us, from Al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bow two rakahs after witr while sitting."
"27089","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umm Al-Hasan, that Umm Salamah narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) measured a span for Fatimah, a span of her waist wrapper."
"27090","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Naim the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a grave be built upon or plastered."
"27091","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Naim the freed slave of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a grave be plastered or built upon or sat upon, my father said: There is no Umm Salamah in it."
"27092","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from Umm Hakim As-Sulamiyyah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters ihram from Bayt Al-Maqdis, Allah will forgive him what preceded of his sin."
"27093","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym the freed slave of the family of Jubayr narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan Al-Akhnasi, from his mother Umm Hakim daughter of Umayyah ibn Al-Akhnas, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever enters ihram from Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa with Umrah or with Hajj, Allah will forgive him what preceded of his sin, he said: So Umm Hakim rode upon that hadith to Bayt Al-Maqdis until she entered ihram from it with Umrah."
"27094","Yunus narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Husayn, from Awf ibn Al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to his wives: The one who will be kind to you after me is the truthful, righteous one, O Allah, give Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise."
"27095","Muhammad ibn Abdullah Abu Ahmad Az-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: My uncle, meaning Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, narrated to me, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, he said: My father resolved upon Umrah, so when his going out came, he said: O my son, if we entered upon the commander and bade him farewell, I said: As you wish, he said: So we entered upon Marwan, and with him were a group among them Abdullah ibn Az-Zubayr, so they mentioned the two rakahs which Ibn Az-Zubayr prays after Asr, so Marwan said to him: From whom did you take them, O son of Az-Zubayr, he said: Abu Hurayrah informed me of them from Aishah, so Marwan sent to Aishah: What two rakahs which Ibn Az-Zubayr mentions that Abu Hurayrah informed him from you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray them after Asr, so she sent to him: Umm Salamah informed me, so he sent to Umm Salamah: What two rakahs, Aishah claims you informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray them after Asr, so she said: May Allah forgive Aishah, she has put my matter in other than its place, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr, and wealth was brought, so he sat dividing it until the caller came to him with Asr, so he prayed Asr, then turned to me, and it was my day, so he bowed two light rakahs, so I said: What are these two rakahs, O Messenger of Allah, were you commanded with them, he said: No, but they are two rakahs I used to bow after Dhuhr, so the division of this wealth kept me until the caller came to me with Asr, so I disliked to leave them, so Ibn Az-Zubayr said: Allah is Greater, did he not pray them one time, by Allah I will never leave them ever, and Umm Salamah said: I did not see him pray them before it nor after it."
"27096","Abu An-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah, meaning Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abd Al-A la, from Abu Sahl of the people of Basra, from Massah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The bleeding woman in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit after her bleeding forty days or forty nights, Abu Khaythamah doubted, and we used to smear wars upon our faces from melasma."
"27097","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast two consecutive months, except he would join Shaban with Ramadan."
"27098","Sulayman ibn Dawud At-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid Al-Hadhdha or Ayyub, from Al-Hasan, he said: Our mother narrated to us, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"27099","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Ya la ibn Mamlak, he said: I asked Umm Salamah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night and his recitation, she said: What is with you and his prayer and his recitation, he used to pray the measure he slept and sleep the measure he prayed, and she was describing his recitation, and it was a recitation explained letter by letter."
"27100","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Jarir ibn Abd Al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Umm Musa, from Umm Salamah, she said: By the One I swear by, Ali was the closest of people in last contact with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: We visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) morning after morning, saying: Ali came repeatedly, she said: And I think he had sent him for a need, she said: So he came after, so I thought he had a need to him, so we went out of the house, so we sat at the door, so I was the nearest of them to the door, so Ali leaned over him and kept whispering to him and conversing privately, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken that day of his, so he was the closest of people to him in last contact."
"27101","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, he said: We heard from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to him, she said: My mother narrated to me, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the khamilah, then I menstruated, so I slipped away from the khamilah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. Then I put on my menstrual clothes and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with him in the khamilah. She said: And I used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a single vessel. She said: And he used to kiss while fasting."
"27102","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us with the like of it in this isnad, except that he said: from a single vessel, from janabah."
"27103","Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdillah, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who drinks in a vessel of silver only gurgles in his belly the Fire of Hell."
"27104","Hasan al-Ashyab narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from al-Saib the freedman of Umm Salamah, that some women from the people of Hims entered upon Umm Salamah, so she asked them: From whom are you? They said: From the people of Hims. Then she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her house, Allah tears away the covering from her."
"27105","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from al-Saib the freedman of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he narrated from Umm Salamah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best prayer of women is in the innermost part of their houses."
"27106","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Hilal narrated to me, from Amr ibn Muslim al-Junda'i, that he said: Ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, and Muhammad ibn Amr, meaning Ibn Alqamah, said, from Amr ibn Muslim ibn Umarah ibn Ukaymah, that he said, if he said it thus, my father said regarding the hadith: Whoever intends to sacrifice, let him not clip nails nor shave anything of his hair in the first ten of Dhu al-Hijjah."
"27107","Talq ibn Ghannam ibn Talq narrated to us, Said ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, from Abu Salih, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, then a nephew of hers entered upon her and prayed two rakahs in her house, then when he prostrated he blew away the dust, so Umm Salamah said to him: Son of my brother, do not blow, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to a boy of his called Yasar, and he blew: Soil your face for Allah."
"27108","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The most I knew to have been brought to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of wealth was a leather pouch in which were eight hundred dirhams."
"27109","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Ali ibn Husayn, he said: Umm Salamah narrated to us, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, then a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the sadaqah of such-and-such? He said: Such-and-such. He said: Then so-and-so transgressed against me. He said: So they looked at him and found him to have transgressed against him by a sa. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So how will it be with you when one who transgresses against you more severely than this transgression strives against you."
"27110","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), why are we not mentioned in the Quran as men are mentioned? She said: Then nothing startled me from him one day except his call upon the minbar: O people. She said: And I was combing my head, so I wrapped my hair, then I drew near to the door and put my hearing at the palm stalk, then I heard him say: Allah Almighty says: Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women, this verse. Affan said: Allah has prepared for them forgiveness and a great reward."
"27111","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salamah narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say often in his supplication: O Allah, Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do hearts indeed turn? He said: Yes, there is no creature of Allah from the children of Adam, of mankind, except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; if Allah Almighty wills He keeps it straight, and if Allah wills He causes it to deviate. So we ask Allah our Lord not to cause our hearts to deviate after He has guided us, and we ask Him to grant us mercy from Himself; indeed He is the Bestower. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not teach me a supplication with which I may supplicate for myself? He said: Yes, say: O Allah, Lord of Muhammad the Prophet, forgive me my sin, remove the rancor of my heart, and protect me from misleading tribulations as long as You keep us alive."
"27112","Abd al-Samad and Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, Affan and Bahz said: al-Anazi, from Umm Salamah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be rulers whom you will recognize and disapprove; whoever disapproves is safe, and whoever hates is absolved, but whoever is pleased and follows. Then he said: Shall we not kill them? He said: No, as long as they pray. And Bahz said: Whoever recognizes is absolved. And Bahz said: Shall we not kill them. And Bahz said in his hadith, he said: Qatadah informed us. And Affan and Bahz said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be."
"27113","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from one of the children of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon the khumrah."
"27114","Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, that Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth; is ghusl upon the woman when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, if she sees water."
"27115","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Husayn, from Awf ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: The one who will show kindness to you after me is the truthful, dutiful one. O Allah, give Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise."
"27116","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: Budayl narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The widow whose husband has died shall not wear saffron-dyed garments, nor reddish garments, nor jewelry, nor dye with henna, nor apply kohl."
"27117","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub and Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Sarraj, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks in a vessel of silver only gurgles in his belly the Fire of Hell."
"27118","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salamah, that she was asked about the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: He used to cut his recitation verse by verse: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment."
"27119","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abd al-Ala, from Abu Sahl, from Mussah al-Azdiyyah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The woman in postpartum used to sit in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forty days, and we used to smear our faces with wars for melasma."
"27120","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Jafar, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"27121","Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, he said: I asked him about the two rakahs after Asr, so he said: I and Abdillah ibn Abbas entered upon Muawiyah, then Muawiyah said: O Ibn Abbas, you have mentioned two rakahs after Asr, and it has reached me that people pray them, and we did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them nor command them. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: That is what Ibn al-Zubayr decides for people. He said: Then Ibn al-Zubayr came and said: What two rakahs by which people decide? Ibn al-Zubayr said: Aishah narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he sent to Aishah two men: The Commander of the Believers greets you and says: What two rakahs which Ibn al-Zubayr claims you commanded him with after Asr? He said: Then Aishah said: That is what Umm Salamah informed him. He said: So we entered upon Umm Salamah and informed her what Aishah said, so she said: May Allah have mercy on her, did I not inform her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them."
"27122","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdillah ibn Zamah narrated to me, from his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, and from his father Abdillah ibn Zamah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: It was my night in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes to me, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Ibn Abi Adi. Abu Ubaydah said: Does this report not strengthen for you the pouring forth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his day before evening."
"27123","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Khalid the freedman of al-Zubayr ibn Nawfal, he said: Zaynab bint Abi Salamah narrated to me, from her mother Umm Salamah, this hadith."
"27124","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdillah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard her say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the prayer is present and supper is present, begin with supper."
"27125","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Ishaq claimed, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib while she was ill, then he said: Will you not go out with us in this journey of ours, intending the Farewell Hajj? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ill and I fear my illness will detain me. He said: Enter ihram for Hajj and say: O Allah, my place of release is where You detain me."
"27126","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Our Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, and guide me to the straightest path."
"27127","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Hasan al-Ahwal, meaning Ali ibn Abd al-Ala, narrated to us, from Abu Sahl, from Mussah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The woman in postpartum in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit after her postpartum forty days or forty nights, and we used to smear wars upon our faces for melasma."
"27128","Surayj narrated to us, Abdillah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then she said: I suffer istihadah. He said: That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. Let her sit the days of her periods, then let her bathe, then let her wrap with a cloth and pray."
"27129","Rawh and Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir ibn Abi Umayyah, brother of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub, then wake fasting."
"27130","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, and she is his maternal aunt, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks in a vessel of silver only gurgles in his belly the Fire of Hell."
"27131","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us, from Layth, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When sins appear in my ummah, Allah Almighty will afflict them all with punishment from Him. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, are there not among them on that day righteous people? He said: Yes. She said: So how will those fare? He said: What befalls the people will befall them, then they will end to forgiveness from Allah and pleasure."
"27132","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covered Ali and Hasan and Husayn and Fatimah with a cloak, then said: O Allah, these are my household and my special ones. O Allah, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Then Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, am I of them? He said: You are toward good."
"27133","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Zuhr, and a delegation came and occupied him, so he did not pray them, then he prayed them after Asr."
"27134","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: By the One who took his soul, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he did not die until most of his prayer was sitting, except the prescribed prayer, and the most beloved deed to him was that which the servant persists upon, even if little."
"27135","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Muaddil Atiyyah al-Tufawi, he said: My father narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, the servant said: Ali and Fatimah are at the doorstep. He said: Stand away from my household. She said: So I stood and withdrew to a side of the house nearby. Then Ali and Fatimah entered, and with them were al-Hasan and al-Husayn, two small boys. Then he took the two boys, kissed them, placed them in his lap, embraced Ali and Fatimah, then covered them with a cloak of his, and said: O Allah, to You, not to the Fire, I and my household. She said: Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, and I? He said: And you."
"27136","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, he said: I entered upon Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, then I said: I will ask you about a matter, and I am shy to ask you about it. She said: Do not be shy, O son of my brother. He said: About approaching women in their backs. She said: Umm Salamah narrated to me that the Ansar did not bend women forward, and the Jews used to say: Whoever bends his wife forward, his child will be cross-eyed. Then when the Muhajirun came to Madinah, they married women of the Ansar and bent them forward, then a woman refused to obey her husband and said to her husband: You shall not do that until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then she entered upon Umm Salamah and mentioned that to her, so she said: Sit until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, the Ansari woman was shy to ask him, so she left. Then Umm Salamah informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Call the Ansari woman. So she was called, then he recited to her this verse: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish, through a single opening."
"27137","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, he said: I heard a freedman of Abu Salamah narrate that he heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he prayed Subh, upon salutation: O Allah, I ask You beneficial knowledge, ample provision, and accepted deed."
"27138","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why are we not mentioned in the Quran as men are mentioned? She said: Then nothing startled me from him that day except his call upon the minbar. She said: And I was combing my hair, so I wrapped my hair, then I went out to a chamber of my house chambers and put my hearing at the palm stalk, and he was saying at the minbar: O people, Allah says in His Book: Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women, to the end of the verse: Allah has prepared for them forgiveness and a great reward."
"27139","He said: Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said, then he mentioned the hadith."
"27140","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I said: By the One who took his soul, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until most of his prayer was sitting, except the prescribed prayer, and the most beloved deed to him was that which the servant persists upon, even if little."
"27141","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be rulers whom you will recognize and disapprove; whoever disapproves is absolved, and whoever hates is safe, but whoever desires and follows. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them? He said: No, as long as they pray the prayer."
"27142","Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"27143","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, he said: Shaqiq narrated to me, and Ibn Numayr said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you attend the sick or the dead, say good, for the angels say amen to what you say. She said: Then when Abu Salamah died, I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I say? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive us and him, and grant me from him a good successor. And Ibn Numayr said: righteous. She said: Then Allah Almighty granted me from him Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27144","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir, brother of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub, then bathe and fast. He said: So Abu Hurayrah retracted his fatwa."
"27145","Yahya and Waki narrated to us, they said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us that he heard Umm Salamah say, Waki said in his hadith, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch his family at night, then wake junub without wet dream, then bathe and fast."
"27146","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Zayd ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who drinks in silver vessels only gurgles in his belly the Fire of Hell."
"27147","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrate to Marwan, he said: Perform wudu from what fire has touched. He said: So Marwan sent to Umm Salamah and asked her, so she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder of meat at my place, then went out to prayer and did not touch water. And my father said: Sufyan did not hear from Abu Awn except this hadith."
"27148","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees water, let her bathe. She said: I said: You have disgraced women; does a woman have a wet dream? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May your right hand be soiled; with what then does her child resemble her."
"27149","Waki narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, I heard it from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was occupied from the two rakahs after Zuhr, so he prayed them after Asr."
"27151","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he left his house said: In the name of Allah, I trust in Allah. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from slipping or straying, or wronging or being wronged, or acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly."
"27152","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Wahb the freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was veiling, so he said: One wrap, not two."
"27153","Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You dispute to me, and I am only a man; perhaps some of you are more eloquent in his plea than others, and I only judge between you according to what I hear. So whomever I judge for him something of his brother's right, let him not take it, for I only cut for him a piece of the Fire which he will bring on the Day of Resurrection."
"27154","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me that Abd al-Hamid ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Amr and al-Qasim informed him that they heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman inform that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that when she came to Madinah she informed them she was the daughter of Abu Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, so they disbelieved her, saying: How the strangers lie, until some people of them set out to Hajj, so they said: What shall you write to your family? So she wrote with them. Then they returned to Madinah confirming her, so she increased in honor with them. She said: Then when I gave birth to Zaynab, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and proposed to me, so I said: One like me is not married; as for me, there is no childbearing in me, and I am jealous and have dependents. He said: I am older than you; as for jealousy, Allah Almighty will remove it; and as for dependents, they are to Allah and His Messenger. So he married her. Then he used to come to her and say: Where is Zunab, until Ammar ibn Yasir came one day and snatched her away, saying: This one prevents the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was nursing her. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Where is Zunab? She said: Quraybah, daughter of Abu Umayyah, and her companion with her, Ammar ibn Yasir took her. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am coming to you tonight. She said: So I stood and took out grains of barley that were in a jar, and took out fat and mashed it for him. She said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night, then in the morning he said when morning came: You have honor with your family; if you wish I will stay seven with you, and if I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"27155","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me that Abd al-Hamid ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Amr and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed him that they heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said, she said: So I put down my baggage and took out grains of barley."
"27156","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon Umm Salamah, so she said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my companions are those who will not see me after they part from me. He said: Then he came to Umar and mentioned that to him. He said: Then Umar came to her and said: I remind you of Allah, am I of them? She said: O Allah, no, and I shall not inform anyone after you."
"27157","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me that Ata ibn Yasar informed him that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that she brought near to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted side, so he ate from it, then stood to prayer and did not perform wudu."
"27158","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abdillah and al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: If you wish I will stay seven with you, and if I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"27159","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: And Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah and Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be overtaken by dawn while junub from his family, then bathe and fast. Ibn Bakr said: The two wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27160","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Yala ibn Mamlak informed me that he asked Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the last Isha, then glorify, then pray after it what Allah Almighty willed of the night, then leave and sleep like what he prayed, then wake from that sleep of his and pray like what he slept, and that last prayer of his would be until dawn."
"27161","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the clamor of disputants at the door of Umm Salamah. She said: So he went out to them and said: You dispute, and I am only a man; perhaps some of you are more knowledgeable of his plea than others, so I judge for him by what I hear from him, thinking him truthful. So whomever I judge for him something of his brother's right, it is a piece of the Fire, so let him take it or leave it."
"27162","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he heard a dispute at the door of his chamber, so he went out to them and said: I am only a man, then he mentioned its meaning."
"27163","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman gifted her a sheep leg given as charity to her, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to accept it."
"27164","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Nabhan the mukatab of Umm Salamah narrated to me, he said: I was leading her at al-Bayda, or he said: at al-Abwa, then she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the mukatab has what to pay, then veil yourself from him."
"27165","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overtaken by dawn junub has no fast. He said: So I and my father set out and entered upon Umm Salamah and Aishah and asked them about that, so they informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub without wet dream, then fast. Then we met Abu Hurayrah, so my father informed him, then the face of Abu Hurayrah changed color, then he said: Thus al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to me, and they are more knowledgeable."
"27166","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from Abdillah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Umm Sulaym, Hajjaj said: wife of Abu Talhah, said: O Messenger of Allah, the woman sees her husband in dream having intercourse with her, is ghusl upon her? He said: Yes, if she sees wetness. Then Umm Salamah said: Does she do that? Then he said: May your right hand be soiled, whence comes resemblance to maternal uncles except from that? Whichever of the two fluids precedes to the womb prevails in resemblance. And Hajjaj said in his hadith: May your forehead be soiled."
"27167","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, do you desire my sister, daughter of Abu Sufyan? He said: What shall I do? She said: You marry her. He said: And is that beloved to you? She said: Yes, I am not alone with you, and the most beloved who shares me in good is my sister. He said: She is not lawful to me. I said: It has reached me you propose Durrah bint Abi Salamah. He said: Daughter of Umm Salamah? She said: Yes. He said: By Allah, had she not been my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful to me; she is the daughter of my brother through nursing; Thuwaybah nursed me and her father. So do not present to me your daughters nor your sisters."
"27168","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah claimed to me that Muawiyah sent to Aishah asking her: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray anything after Asr? She said: As for with me, no, but Umm Salamah informed me he did that, so send to her and ask her. So he sent to Umm Salamah, so she said: Yes, he entered upon me after Asr and prayed two prostrations. I said: O Prophet of Allah, was something revealed to you regarding these two prostrations? He said: No, but I prayed Zuhr and was occupied, so I made them up after Asr."
"27169","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from al-Hakam, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every intoxicant and enervant."
"27170","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Kathir informed me, from Ibn Safinah, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No servant is afflicted with calamity and says: We belong to Allah and to Him we return, O Allah reward me in my calamity and replace for me better than it, except Allah rewards him in his calamity and replaces for him better than it. She said: Then when Abu Salamah died, I said: Who is better than Abu Salamah, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Then Allah Almighty resolved for me, so I said it: O Allah reward me in my calamity and replace for me better than it. She said: Then I married the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27171","Yala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about women's hems. He said: A handspan. Then I said: Then their feet will show, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then a forearm, do not exceed it."
"27172","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Some companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Salamah and said: O Mother of the Believers, narrate to us of the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His secret and open were alike. Then I regretted and said: I have divulged the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Then when he entered, she informed him, so he said: You did well."
"27173","Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu Sahl of Basra, from Mussah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The woman in postpartum in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit after her postpartum forty days or forty nights. She said: And we used to smear wars upon our faces for melasma."
"27174","Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about gold bound with it, or musk bound with it. He said: Make it silver and yellow it with some saffron."
"27175","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hunaydah al-Khuzai narrated to us, from his mother, she said: I entered upon Umm Salamah and asked her about fasting. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command me to fast three days of every month: the first of them Monday, and Friday, and Thursday."
"27176","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with five or seven, not separating between them with speech nor salutation."
"27177","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, the sons of Abu Salamah are in my care, and they have nothing except what I spend upon them, and I shall not leave them thus nor thus; is there reward for me if I spend upon them? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spend upon them, for you have the reward of what you spend upon them."
"27178","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Sabit, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, my father said, and in another place: Mamar, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman asked her about the man who approaches his wife bent forward, so Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish, through a single opening."
"27179","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Sabit, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, my father said, and in another place: Mamar, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman asked her about the man who approaches his wife bent forward, so Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish, through a single opening."
"27180","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he gave salutation remained a little, and they used to see that was so women would pass before men."
"27181","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray after Asr ever except once: people came to him after Zuhr and occupied him with something, so he did not pray after Zuhr anything until he prayed Asr. She said: Then when he prayed Asr, he entered my house and prayed two rakahs."
"27182","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while fasting, and they used to bathe in a single vessel."
"27183","Ismail narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was quicker in hastening Zuhr than you, and you are quicker in hastening Asr than him."
"27184","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir, brother of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub without wet dream, then fast his day. He said: So Abu Hurayrah abandoned his fatwa."
"27185","Ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir ibn Abi Umayyah, brother of Umm Salamah, and he did not mention Umm Salamah, the like of it."
"27186","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid narrate, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: The transgressing party will kill you."
"27187","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: I asked Abdillah ibn al-Harith about the two rakahs after Asr, so he said: We were with Muawiyah, then he narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray them. So Muawiyah sent to Aishah, and I was among them, so we asked her, so she said: I did not hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but Umm Salamah narrated to me. Then I asked her, so Umm Salamah narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, then something was brought and he began dividing it until Asr prayer came, so he stood and prayed Asr, then prayed after it two rakahs. Then when he prayed them, he said: These two rakahs I used to pray after Zuhr. Then Umm Salamah said: And I had informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them. He said: So I came to Muawiyah and informed him of that, so Ibn al-Zubayr said: Has he not prayed them? I shall not cease praying them. Then Muawiyah said to him: You are indeed contentious; you will not cease loving dissent as long as you live."
"27188","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Nafi, he said: I heard Zaynab bint Abi Salamah narrate, from her mother, that a woman whose husband died and they feared for her eye, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought permission for kohl. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you used to be in her house in her shabbiest clothes, or in the worst of her shabby clothes, in her house for a year; then when a dog passed she threw a dung and went out. So not four months and ten days."
"27189","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would not fast a complete month of the year known except Shaban, joining it with Ramadan."
"27190","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Umar or Amr ibn Muslim, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever intends to sacrifice in the crescent of Dhu al-Hijjah, let him not take of his hair and nails."
"27191","Ismail ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Umar ibn Muslim ibn Ammar ibn Ukaymah narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, then he mentioned the hadith."
"27192","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Nabhan, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the mukatab finds what to pay, then veil yourselves from him."
"27193","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Khalil, from Safinah the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him began to say: Prayer, prayer, and what your right hands possess. So he kept speaking with it, and his tongue could hardly utter it."
"27194","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, brother of Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas differed regarding the widow when she delivers her burden. Abu Hurayrah said: She may marry. And Ibn Abbas said: The farther of the two terms. He said: So they sent to Umm Salamah, so she said: The husband of Subayah bint al-Harith died, then she gave birth after his death by fifteen nights. Then two men proposed to her. He said: So she inclined to one of them. Then when they feared she would decide for herself to one of them, they said: You have not become lawful. So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You have become lawful, so marry whom you wish."
"27195","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, he said: Abd al-Rahman entered upon Umm Salamah, so she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my companions are those who will not see me after I die ever. He said: So Abd al-Rahman left her frightened until he entered upon Umar, so he said to him: Hear what your mother says. So Umar stood until he came to her, then entered upon her and asked her, then said: I adjure you by Allah, am I of them? She said: No, and I shall not absolve anyone after you."
"27196","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdillah ibn Zamah informed me that his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him that her mother Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to say: All other wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to admit upon them anyone by that nursing, and they said to Aishah: By Allah, we see this only as a concession which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted to Salim specially. So no one by this nursing shall enter upon us, nor see us."
"27197","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Abu Iyad narrated that Marwan sent to Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent to her his freedman, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub, then fast and not break. He said: So he returned to him and informed him. He said: So he sent to Aishah, so he sent to her his freedman or his boy Dhakwan, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub from intercourse, not wet dream, then fast and not break. Then he said to him: Go to Abu Hurayrah and inform him. So he went to Abu Hurayrah and informed him from Umm Salamah and from Aishah, so he said: They are more knowledgeable."
"27198","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Iyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah and Aishah. He said: So I met her boy Nafi and sent him to her and he asked her. He said: So he returned to me and informed me that she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub and wake fasting. He said: Then he sent me to Aishah, so I met her boy Dhakwan and sent him to her, so he returned to me and informed me that she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub from intercourse without wet dream, then wake fasting. He said: So I came to Marwan and informed him, so he said: I adjure you, you shall come to Abu Hurayrah and inform him of it. So I came to him and informed him, so he said: They are more knowledgeable."
"27199","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Iyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah and Aishah, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Then he met the boy of Aishah, Dhakwan Abu Amr, and said: I met Nafi, boy of Umm Salamah."
"27200","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Umm Salamah and Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that dawn used to overtake him while junub from his family, then he would bathe and fast."
"27201","Rawh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Aishah, she informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wake up junub in Ramadan from his wife, then he would bathe and fast."
"27202","Rawh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Umm Salamah, she informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wake up junub, then he would fast his day."
"27203","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Whoever wakes up junub without a wet dream, let him not fast. So Abu Bakr and his father Abd al-Rahman went until they entered upon Umm Salamah and Aishah, and both of them said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wake up junub without a wet dream, then he would fast. Then Abu Bakr and his father Abd al-Rahman went and came to Marwan and narrated to him. Then he said: I urge you both to go to Abu Hurayrah and narrate to him. So they went to Abu Hurayrah and informed him. He said: Did they both say it to you. They said: Yes. He said: They both know better; al-Fadl ibn Abbas only informed me of it."
"27204","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, he said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me at Mina, from his father, that Umm Salamah said: Abu Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return; with You I seek the reward of my calamity, reward me in it and replace for me what is better than it. When Abu Salamah was dying, he said: O Allah, leave me behind in my family with good. When he died, I said: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return; O Allah, with You I seek the reward of my calamity, so reward me in it. She said: And I wanted to say: and replace for me better than it, so I said: And who is better than Abu Salamah. I kept on until I said it. When her waiting period ended, Abu Bakr proposed to her and she rejected him, then Umar proposed to her and she rejected him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to her, so she said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and to his messenger; inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I am a jealous woman, and that I am a woman with children, and that none of my guardians is present. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to her: As for your saying that I am a woman with children, Allah will suffice you your children; and as for your saying that I am jealous, I shall supplicate to Allah to remove your jealousy; and as for the guardians, there is none of them present or absent except that he will approve of me. I said: O Umar, stand and marry the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed I shall not deprive you of anything of what I gave your sister so-and-so: two millstones, two jars, and a cushion of leather stuffed with fiber. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to her, and when he came she would take Zaynab and put her in her lap to nurse her, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shy and generous and would feel shy, so he would leave. He did that several times, then Ammar ibn Yasir noticed what she was doing, so he came one day, and Ammar came, and he was her brother through her mother, and he entered upon her and snatched her from her lap and said: Leave this ill-favored wretched one by whom you have harmed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and entered, and he began to turn his gaze in the house and say: Where is Zanab, what has Zanab done. She said: Ammar came and took her away. He said: Then he consummated with his wife, then he said: If you wish I shall stay seven with you, I stay seven for the wives. Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me; and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah, mursal."
"27205","Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me; and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah, mursal."
"27206","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab daughter of Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there reward for me for spending on the sons of Abi Salamah, for I shall not leave them thus and thus, they are only my sons. He said: Yes, for you is reward for what you spend on them."
"27207","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: Ribi ibn Hirash narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me with a gloomy face. She said: So I thought that was from pain, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you gloomy-faced, is it from pain. He said: No, but the seven dinars that were brought to us yesterday, we reached evening and did not spend them, I forgot them in the seam of the bedding."
"27208","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from a woman of them, that she asked Umm Salamah about nabidh, so she said: Every intoxicant is forbidden; and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzaffat, and dubba, and hantam."
"27209","Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Qasim, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"27210","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him, that Abu Salamah informed him, that he and Ibn Abbas met at Abu Hurayrah, so they sent Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salamah to ask her. Then Umm Salamah mentioned that Subayah al-Aslamiyyah lost her husband, then she gave birth nights after him. Subayah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he commanded her to marry."
"27211","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, he said: Umm Salamah narrated to us, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the prayer comes and supper comes, begin with supper."
"27212","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who braids the hair of my head tightly, shall I undo it for ghusl from janabah. He said: It suffices you only three handfuls you pour upon your head."
"27213","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Asr, then entered my house and prayed two rakahs. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed a prayer you did not used to pray. He said: Wealth came to me and distracted me from the two rakahs I used to bow after Zuhr, so I prayed them now. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we make them up when missed. He said: No."
"27214","Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Abu Kab, the owner of silk, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: I said to Umm Salamah: O Mother of the Believers, what was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was with you. She said: His most frequent supplication was: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, how frequent is your supplication: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. He said: O Umm Salamah, there is no human except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; whatever He wills He keeps upright, and whatever He wills He turns away. Abdullah said: I asked my father about Abu Kab, so he said: Trustworthy, and his name is Abd Rabbihi ibn Ubayd."
"27215","Muadh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I have not forgotten it, the day of al-Khandaq, when his chest had become dusty while he was handing them the milk and saying: O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. He said: Then Ammar came, and when he saw him he said: Woe to you, son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you. He said: Then I narrated it to Muhammad, so he said: from his mother; indeed she used to visit the Mother of the Believers."
"27216","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how about women. He said: They let down a span. I said: Then it would be uncovered from them, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then a forearm, let them not exceed it."
"27217","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata informed us, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: She put locks of gold on her neck, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and turned away from her. So I said: Will you not look at her adornment. He said: From your adornment I turn away. He said: They claimed that he said: It would not harm one of you if she made an earring of silver then colored it with saffron."
"27218","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi informed me, that Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, that Umm Salamah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, swore not to enter upon some of his wives for a month. When twenty-nine days passed, he came to them in the morning or evening. So it was said to him: You swore, O Prophet of Allah, not to enter upon them for a month. He said: Indeed the month is twenty-nine days."
"27219","Rawh narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Safinah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, narrated, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the general bequest of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at his death was: Prayer, prayer, and what your right hands possess, until the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began to murmur it in his chest and his tongue could not utter it."
"27220","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: My Lord, forgive and have mercy and guide me to the straightest path."
"27221","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: An umm walad of Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, she said: I was a woman with a long train, and I used to come to the mosque dragging it. So I asked Umm Salamah, I said: I am a woman whose train is long, and I come to the mosque dragging it over a filthy place, then I drag it over a clean place. So Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it passes over the filthy place then passes over the clean place, that is purification."
"27222","Rawh narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating, from Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah, from Umm Salamah, that Abu Bakr went out trading to Busra, with him Nuayman and Suwaybit ibn Harmalah, both of them Badri, and Suwaybit was in charge of provisions. Nuayman came to him and said: Feed me. He said: No, until Abu Bakr comes. Nuayman was a laughing jesting man, so he said: I shall surely anger you. He went to people who had brought camels and said: Buy from me an Arab lad, handsome, eloquent, and perhaps he will say: I am free; if you will abandon him for that, then leave me, do not spoil my lad for me. They said: Rather we shall buy him from you for ten young she-camels. He came driving them and came with the people until he hobbled them, then he said to the people: There he is, this is he. The people came and said: We have bought you. Suwaybit said: He is lying, I am a free man. They said: He already informed us of your story. They threw the rope around his neck and took him away. Abu Bakr came and was informed, so he and companions of his went and returned the she-camels and took him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions around him laughed at it for a year."
"27223","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Hind daughter of al-Harith al-Qurashiyyah narrated to me, that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed her, that women in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he gave salam from the obligatory prayer, would stand, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would remain, and those who prayed of the men would remain as long as Allah willed. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, the men would stand."
"27224","Abd al-Samad and Harami, in meaning, narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Khalil, from a companion of his, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be disagreement at the death of a caliph, so a man will come out of Madinah fleeing to Makkah. People of Makkah will come to him and bring him out while he dislikes it, and they will pledge to him between the Corner and the Maqam. An army from Sham will be sent to them and will be swallowed at al-Bayda. When people see that, the abdal of Sham and the groups of Iraq will come to him and pledge to him. Then a man of Quraysh will arise whose maternal uncles are Kalb, so the Makkan will send an expedition to him, and they will prevail over them, and that is the expedition of Kalb; and deprivation is for whoever does not witness the spoils of Kalb. He will divide wealth and apply among people the sunnah of their Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Islam will lay its chest upon the earth. He will remain nine years; Harami said: or seven."
"27225","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke from his sleep saying: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with you. He said: A group of my ummah will be swallowed, then they will be sent to a man, so he will come to Makkah, and Allah will protect him from them, and they will be swallowed; their place of perishing is one, and their sources are diverse. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how can their place of perishing be one while their sources are diverse. He said: Among them is one coerced, so he comes coerced."
"27226","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned its meaning."
"27227","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Qays, the freed slave of Amr ibn al-As, he said: I said to Umm Salamah: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kiss while fasting. She said: No. I said: Aishah informs people that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss while fasting. She said: I said: Perhaps he could not control himself from her out of love; as for me, no."
"27228","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Haywah and Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, they said: We heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib saying: Abu Imran narrated to me, he said: Umm Salamah said to me: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O family of Muhammad, whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter ihram in his Hajj, or in his Hajjah; Abu Abd al-Rahman doubted."
"27229","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon Umm Salamah and said: O Mother of the Believers, I fear I have perished; I am among the wealthiest of Quraysh, I sold land of mine for forty thousand dinars. She said: Spend, O my son, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among my companions is one who will not see me after I leave him. So I came to Umar and informed him, so he came to her and said: By Allah, am I of them. She said: O Allah, no, and I shall not absolve anyone after you."
"27230","Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid informed me, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: There was no garment more beloved to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than a shirt."
"27231","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abi Awn, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Marwan said: How can we ask anyone while among us are the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he sent to Umm Salamah, and she informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to prayer, so she picked out for him a shoulder from a pot, and he ate it, then went out and prayed."
"27232","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me at Mina, from his father, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is struck by a calamity, let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return; O Allah, with You I seek the reward of my calamity, so reward me in it and replace for me with better than it. When Abu Salamah died, I said it, and whenever I reached: and replace for me with better than it, I said in myself: And who is better than Abu Salamah. Then I said it. When her waiting period ended, Abu Bakr sent to her proposing to her, but she did not marry him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Umar ibn al-Khattab proposing her for him. She said: Inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I am a jealous woman, and that I am a woman with children, and none of my guardians is present. He came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said: Return to her and say to her: As for your saying that I am a jealous woman, I shall supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to remove your jealousy; and as for your saying that I am a woman with children, your children will be sufficed; and as for your saying that none of your guardians is present, there is none of your guardians present or absent who dislikes that."
"27233","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sabit, from Hafsah daughter of Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Muhajirun came to Madinah to the Ansar, they married of their women, and the Muhajirun used to practice jabb, and the Ansar did not practice tajbiyah. A man of the Muhajirun wanted his wife for that, but she refused him until she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: So she came to him but was shy to ask him, so Umm Salamah asked him. Then was revealed: Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish. And he said: Not except in one valve. And Waki said: Ibn Sabit is a man of Quraysh."
"27234","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab daughter of Umm Salamah, from her mother, she said: A mukhannath said to her brother Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah: If Allah grants you conquest of Taif tomorrow, I shall point you to the daughter of Ghaylan, for she comes with four and goes with eight. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard him and said: Expel these from your houses, let them not enter upon you."
"27235","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: from one who heard Umm Salamah narrating, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say at the end of Fajr when he prayed: O Allah, I ask You beneficial knowledge, accepted deed, and good provision."
"27236","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say when he prayed Subh upon giving salam, then he mentioned it."
"27237","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abi Yunus al-Bahili, he said: I heard Muhajir al-Makki, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: An army will raid the House, until when they are at a desert of the earth they will be swallowed. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the coerced of them. He said: He will be raised upon his intention."
"27238","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, from Zaynab daughter of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the khamilah, I menstruated, so I slipped away and took my menstrual clothes. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Have you menstruated. I said: Yes. So he called me and I lay with him in the khamilah. She and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe from one vessel from janabah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss her while fasting."
"27239","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hudbah narrated it to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, with the isnad of this hadith and its meaning."
"27240","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he left his house, said: In Your name, my Lord, I seek refuge in You from slipping, or going astray, or wronging, or being wronged, or being ignorant, or being treated ignorantly."
"27241","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The legs of the minbar are watered in Paradise."
"27242","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Sabit, from Hafsah daughter of Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said regarding His statement, Mighty and Majestic: Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish: He said: One valve."
"27243","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sad, he said: Bukayr narrated to me, from Abi Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zaynab daughter of Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kissed while fasting."
"27244","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Bukayr narrated to me, from Abi Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Abi Salamah, then he mentioned the same with its isnad."
"27245","Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not die until most of his prayer was sitting except the obligatory, and the most beloved deed to him was what the servant persists upon even if little."
"27246","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan, he said: I heard Aba Awn saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaddad saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Ablution is from what fire touched. So I mentioned that, or he mentioned that, to Marwan. He said: I do not know whom we ask, while among us are the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he sent me to Umm Salamah, and she narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to prayer, then he took a shank and bit meat from a bone, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"27247","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said ibn Jumhan, from Safinah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, he said: Umm Salamah freed me and stipulated upon me to serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as long as he lived."
"27248","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ammar ibn Abi Muawiyah al-Bajali, from Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she used to bathe, she and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from janabah from one vessel."
"27249","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, and she brought out to us hair of the hair of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dyed with henna and katam."
"27250","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Zaynab daughter of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she arrived while ill, so she mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Circumambulate behind the people while riding. She said: So I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while at the Kabah reciting al-Tur. My father said: And I read it to Abd al-Rahman. She said: So I circumambulated while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was then praying beside the House, reciting al-Tur and a book inscribed."
"27251","He said: It was read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said ibn Qays, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he said: Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah were asked about the woman whose husband died. Ibn Abbas said: The later of the two terms; and Abu Hurayrah said: When she gives birth she becomes lawful. So Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman entered upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked her about that. She said: Subayah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth after the death of her husband by half a month. Two men proposed to her, one young and the other old. She inclined to the young one. The old one said: She is not lawful. Her family was absent, and he hoped when her family came they would prefer him. So she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish."
"27252","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a woman used to bleed heavily in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought a fatwa for her. He said: Let her consider the number of nights and days she used to menstruate of the month before what befell her befell her, let her leave prayer that amount of the month; when she reaches that, let her bathe, then let her bind with a cloth, then pray."
"27253","Waki narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salamah, she said: Two men of the Ansar came disputing to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over inheritances between them that had become effaced, with no proof between them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You dispute to me, and I am only a human; perhaps some of you is more eloquent in his plea, or he said: in his plea, than another. I judge between you upon what I hear. Whoever I judge for him something of his brother's right, let him not take it, for I only cut for him a piece of Fire; he will come with it as a yoke on his neck on the Day of Resurrection. The two men wept, and each one of them said: My right is for my brother. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Since you both said so, go and divide, then seek the truth, then cast lots, then let each one of you absolve his companion."
"27254","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: The most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was what is persisted upon even if little."
"27255","Waki narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Farrukh, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss me while fasting and I fasting."
"27256","Waki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah, the freed slave of al-Sahba, narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: And let them not disobey you in good; he said: Wailing."
"27257","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Sufayra narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, son of the daughter of Umm Salamah, narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, that when Abu Salamah died leaving her and her waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, proposed to her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have three traits: I am an old woman. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am older than you. She said: And I am a jealous woman. He said: I shall supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to remove your jealousy from you. She said: O Messenger of Allah, and I am a woman with children. He said: They are to Allah and to His Messenger. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her. He said: He came to her and found her nursing, so he left. Then he came to her and found her nursing, so he left. He said: That reached Ammar ibn Yasir, so he came to her and said: You have come between the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his need; bring the girl. He said: So he took her and sought a wet nurse for her. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to her and said: Where is Zunab, meaning Zaynab. She said: O Messenger of Allah, Ammar took her. So he entered with her and said: Indeed your being with your family is honorable. He said: He stayed with her till evening, then he said: If you wish I shall stay seven for you, and if I stay seven for you I shall stay seven for the rest of my wives; and if you wish I shall apportion for you. She said: No, rather apportion for me."
"27258","He narrated to us."
"27259","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, son of the daughter of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that it reached her that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim afflicted with a calamity who says: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return; O Allah, reward me in my calamity and replace for me with better than it, except that it will be done for him. She said: So I said this, and Allah rewarded me in my calamity; so who will replace for me the place of Abu Salamah. When her waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, proposed to her."
"27260","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Tahla, he said: I said to Abi Salamah: Your foster brother Sulaym does not perform ablution from what fire touched. He said: So he struck the chest of Sulaym and said: I bear witness upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she used to bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to perform ablution from what fire touched."
"27261","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with seven or five, not separating between them with speech or salam."
"27262","Affan narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Umm Salamah, Mother of the Believers, she said: By the One Who took his soul, he did not die until most of his prayer was while sitting, and the most beloved deeds to him was the righteous deed the servant persists upon even if little."
"27263","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abi al-Khalil, from Safinah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while dying: Prayer, prayer, and what your right hands possess. He kept speaking it and could not utter."
"27264","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There will be rulers who recognize and deny; whoever recognizes is absolved, and whoever denies is safe, but whoever approves and follows. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight their likes. He said: No, as long as they pray."
"27265","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he left his house, said: In the name of Allah. Shubah said: To the best of my knowledge he said it. He said: And Sufyan mentioned it from him, and there is no doubt in the rest: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from going astray, or slipping, or wronging, or being ignorant, or being treated ignorantly."
"27266","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Aba Ishaq, that he heard Aba Salamah narrating, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not die until most of his prayer was sitting except the obligatory, and the most beloved deed to him was the most persistent even if little."
"27267","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say when he prayed Subh upon giving salam: O Allah, I ask You beneficial knowledge, good provision, and accepted deed."
"27268","Waki narrated to us, Harun al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he read: Indeed he did unrighteous deed."
"27269","Waki narrated to us, Harun al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he read: Indeed he did unrighteous deed."
"27270","Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about gold binding musk, or tied. He said: Make it silver and color it with something of saffron."
"27271","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, she said: I wore a necklace with hairs of gold. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw it and turned away from me and said: What assures you from Allah adorning you in its place on the Day of Resurrection with hairs of Fire. She said: So I removed it."
"27272","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, men raid and we do not raid, and we have half the inheritance. So Allah revealed: And do not wish for what Allah has favored some of you with over others."
"27273","Affan narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she showed me hair of the hair of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dyed with henna and katam."
"27274","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with thirteen; when he grew old and weak, he prayed witr with seven."
"27275","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Wail, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you attend the dead or the sick, say good, for the angels say amen to what you say."
"27276","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, the freed slave of Ibn Umar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, that Fatimah had prolonged bleeding and used to bathe in a basin of hers, then come out with yellowness and murkiness high. Umm Salamah sought a fatwa for her from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: She waits the days of her recitation or the days of her menstruation, leaving prayer therein, and bathes in other than that, and binds with a cloth, and prays."
"27277","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Awn informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had narrating, he said: Marwan said: How can we ask anyone about a thing while among us are the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he sent to Umm Salamah and asked her. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, so I picked out for him a shoulder from a pot, and he ate of it, then went out to prayer."
"27278","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salamah, that the recitation of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was, then she described: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, letter by letter, slow recitation. Affan cut his recitation."
"27279","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Khalid, meaning al-Hadhdha, narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Umm Salamah, that she was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a blanket, then menstruation befell her. He said: Stand, wrap yourself, then return."
"27280","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abi Salih, that Umm Salamah saw a relative of hers blowing when he wanted to prostrate. She said: Do not blow, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a lad of ours called Rabah: Soil your face, O Rabah."
"27281","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said, meaning Ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir ibn Abi Umayyah, from his sister Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wake up junub, then fast and not break."
"27282","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Fatimah: Bring me your husband and your two sons. She brought them, so he cast over them a Fadak cloak. He said: Then he placed his hand upon them, then he said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so make Your prayers and blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Umm Salamah said: So I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hand and said: You are upon good."
"27283","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Abi Saghir narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyyah, from Umm Salamah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: A people raiding this House will surely be swallowed at a desert of the earth. A man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, even if among them is the coerced. He said: Every man of them will be raised upon his intention."
"27284","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Abdullah al-Jadali, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said to me: Is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reviled among you. I said: Allah forbid, or Glory be to Allah, or a word like it. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever reviles Ali has reviled me."
"27285","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yazid, and he is Abu Shuja, informed us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj saying: Naim, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, narrated to me, that Umm Salamah was asked: Does a woman bathe with a man. She said: Yes, if she is clever. I saw myself and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathing from one basin; we pour upon our hands until we clean them, then we pour water upon ourselves."
"27286","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali informed me, he said: My father narrated to us, from Kurayb, that he heard Umm Salamah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast Saturday and Sunday more than he fasted of the days, and he would say: They are the festivals of the polytheists, and I love to oppose them."
